      "severity": "high",
      "description": "The function appends values to the store before checking for a negative value. If a negative value occurs later in the batch, the store has already been modified, which violates the contract that the store must remain unchanged if any value is negative.",
      "evidence": "Example: store = [1], values = [2, -3, 4]. Candidate appends 2, then raises ValueError on -3, leaving store as [1, 2] instead of unchanged [1]."
    }
  ]
}
